{#- B-2 executive summary: one macro per paragraph (worked example, section 1).
    Every argument that prints a value is a slot placeholder from
    b2_narrative.Writer; code fills it. Arguments ending in _n are plain numbers
    used only to choose singular or plural, and are never printed. The literal
    text holds no digits and no number words. A line starting "- " is a bullet;
    the report renders a paragraph's bullets as a list. -#}

{% macro verdict(facility, date, start, duration, run_status_phrase, final_status) -%}
{{ facility }} was inspected{% if date %} on {{ date }}{% endif %}{% if start %}, beginning at {{ start }}{% endif %}{% if duration %} and running for {{ duration }}{% endif %}. The run {{ run_status_phrase }} and closed with an overall result of {{ final_status }}.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro empty() -%}
No checkpoints were recorded for this run.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro results(passed, passed_n, failed, warned, warned_n) -%}
{{ passed }} checkpoint{{ "" if passed_n == 1 else "s" }} returned PASS{% if warned_n %}, {{ warned }} returned WARN{% endif %} and {{ failed }} returned FAIL.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro failed_lead() -%}
The failed checkpoints, grouped by what was recorded at them:
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro failed_group(has_evidence, findings, names) -%}
- {{ "Captured evidence images" if has_evidence else "Captured no evidence images" }}, {% if findings %}with findings of {{ findings }}{% else %}with no findings logged{% endif %}: {{ names }}.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro finding(feature, severity) -%}
{{ feature }} ({{ severity }})
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro contradiction_pointer() -%}
The record's own counts disagree with its data; both are set out in the coverage statement.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro gap_pointer(label) -%}
{{ label }} was not recorded on this run; see the coverage statement.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro measurement(field, zone, value, n, n_n, source) -%}
The highest mean {{ field }} was recorded in zone {{ zone }}, at {{ value }} across {{ n }} {{ source }}{{ "" if n_n == 1 else "s" }}.
{%- endmacro %}
